    "evidence": [
      "CSPProvider exports native Props and State types and a type namespace based on the pinned React declaration. Its context now supplies nonce and disableStyleElements to the shared scrollbar style element in Scroll Area and Select. Direct Chromium probes show a default style tag, the requested nonce, and no tag when disabled for both component families. renderElement reads the initial render function with untrack, while merged props remain reactive. Full behavior review remains pending.",
      "useMediaQuery now supports the pinned defaultMatches, matchMedia, ssrMatchMedia, and noSsr options, strips an @media prefix, and removes its listener. Two native client tests and two native server tests pass; full original behavior review remains pending."
    ]
  },
